From c3c41336ce509312a7c30db33abff9e4cbac524c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Heimersheim <stefan.heimersheim@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 23:16:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] mptcp: do not re-inject the unacked window on stale
 subflows with the redundant scheduler

When the path manager marks a subflow stale (no progress for
stale_loss_cnt retransmit timeouts while another subflow is healthy),
mptcp_pm_nl_subflow_chk_stale() re-injects the whole unacked window via
__mptcp_retransmit_pending_data(), because with a single-subflow-per-round
scheduler the data queued on the stale subflow exists nowhere else.

With the redundant scheduler every other active subflow has already been
handed that data, or catches up on it the next time it can send (see
__subflow_push_redundant()). Re-injecting it again makes the healthy links
carry the unacked window a third time. In the netns test (20 ms RTT,
100 Mbit paths, 30 % loss on one path) this showed up as the healthy path
transmitting 149 % of the payload instead of ~107 %.

Skip the re-injection for redundant connections; the stale marking itself
and the MPTCP_MIB_SUBFLOWSTALE accounting are unchanged, and the
msk-level retransmit timer still covers the case where no subflow carried
a range.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/mptcp/pm_netlink.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/pm_netlink.c b/net/mptcp/pm_netlink.c
index 7ea8ccd16..b5dcd3d69 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/pm_netlink.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/pm_netlink.c
@@ -1355,7 +1355,14 @@ void mptcp_pm_nl_subflow_chk_stale(const struct mptcp_sock *msk, struct sock *ss
 			slow = lock_sock_fast(ssk);
 			if (!tcp_rtx_and_write_queues_empty(ssk)) {
 				subflow->stale = 1;
-				__mptcp_retransmit_pending_data(sk);
+				/* With the redundant scheduler the other subflows
+				 * already carry (or catch up on) everything this
+				 * one has queued; re-injecting the whole unacked
+				 * window would only duplicate it once more on the
+				 * healthy links.
+				 */
+				if (!mptcp_sched_is_redundant(msk))
+					__mptcp_retransmit_pending_data(sk);
 				MPTCP_INC_STATS(net, MPTCP_MIB_SUBFLOWSTALE);
 			}
 			unlock_sock_fast(ssk, slow);
